# Public origin of the deployed site. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph
# metadata, robots.txt and the sitemap. The production build REFUSES to run
# without it, because the value is baked in at build time and cannot be
# corrected at runtime.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://raymarnuts.com pnpm build
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the ONLY environment variable the site has.
#
# The site is deployed as a static export to shared LiteSpeed/Apache hosting,
# so nothing runs on the server that could read an environment at request time.
# Everything else that used to live here is now configured in the files that
# are actually deployed:
#
#   Quotation delivery  → QUOTE_TO_EMAIL / QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL at the top of
#                         `public/teklif-gonder.php`. Set one before launch:
#                         with neither, the endpoint returns 503 and the form
#                         shows its error state. That is deliberate — a visitor
#                         told the message failed can phone instead, whereas
#                         one told it succeeded cannot.
#
#   Security headers    → `public/.htaccess`. `next.config.ts` no longer emits
#                         them; a static export never consults its own routes
#                         manifest, so they would silently disappear.
#
#   HTTPS on the LAN    → no longer applicable. HSTS and
#                         `upgrade-insecure-requests` come from `.htaccess` on
#                         the host, so a local production build over plain HTTP
#                         is not affected by them and `ALLOW_INSECURE_LAN` is
#                         gone. Preview a build with:
#
#                           pnpm build && node scripts/serve-static.mjs out 3100
